    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131-a17">

                <pb facs="0253" n="907" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg907"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 11 in 2 in No. 219.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Glarvecke to Mr. Mix</hi>.</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[Postal card.]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Mix</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rio Grande City, Texas:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Tell some officer to tell General Hatch to
                    watch Los Cuevas and immediate crossings, as upward of 150 thieves have gone up
                    to rendezvous at that place, to make a big raid. They intended to dash on
                    Brownsville three nights, but it was frustrated by our vigilance.</p>
                <p>More anon.</p>
                <p>Yours fraternally,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. GLARVECKE.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-03-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi> 8, 1875</date>. Received 3
                        p.m. March 10.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
